# Line endings are a determinism concern here, not a style preference.
#
# This repository hashes content directly. `MathCertificate.certificate_hash`,
# `DreEvidenceEnvelope.payload_hash`, and the formula-index canonical digests
# are all computed over exact bytes, and `write_dre_experiment` produces the
# artifact that DRE consumes. DRE in turn computes `ModelHash` over the raw
# bytes of a pack, so the CRLF and LF versions of the same file are different
# models.
#
# A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` and no pin here would produce
# different hashes from a Linux CI checkout of the same commit, and every
# cross-machine replay would fail while every file looked identical in every
# editor.
#
# So: normalise everything to LF in the repository and in the working tree.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Research state, DRE artifacts, and model packs are hashed byte-for-byte.
# Pinning them explicitly means a future change to the blanket rule above
# cannot quietly change what a stored hash refers to.
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

*.py   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.cfg  text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.bin  binary
